  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **The law** (`crates/sim/src/verify/excess.rs`). `excess_floor` reads a model's chord error `c` in three ranges:\n  - `c` up to `DEV_TOL` (0.01 mm): the whole excess is taken (#864, no change).\n  - `c` from 0.01 mm to `WIDE_CHORD_LIMIT` (0.02 mm): only the promised chord (0.005 mm) is taken. The program verdict is then read at the model's own chord error.\n  - `c` over 0.02 mm: the whole excess is taken, so nothing is left. The operation is refused by name.\n- `WIDE_CHORD_LIMIT` is a constant. No file, facet budget or vouch can raise it.\n- A tolerance is never made larger than the law's own tolerance.\n- **Collision bands** grow by the whole excess (`verify::band_growth`). The widening is never given to a band.\n- **Strict readers** keep #864's law (`verify::strict_floor`, `fidelity_law::tightened_strict`):\n  - the turning margin, the lathe axial-hole tolerance and `revolve::gouge_tol_on`;\n  - the rotary field allowances;\n  - the probe stylus slack.\n\n  The program gate reads the strict law for these kinds (`fidelity_law::widens`).\n- **Header note.** `ProgramId` has `notes`. The engine writes each note through the script's `onComment`, after `onOpen`. `document_program_id` fills the notes from `fidelity_note::program_notes`. Example: `Reduced accuracy: model brick was checked to 0.019 mm, not 0.010 mm`.\n- **Notes in plain words.** The model summary, the MCP `facts` note and the #2994 import note (`step::loosened_consequence`) say the same fact.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2996-wide-verdict.md`. It gives the rule for each direction, each reader, what the user loses, and what was dropped.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe #864 law took the whole excess from each tolerance. At a chord of 0.02 mm the excess is 0.015 mm. That is more than `DEV_TOL`, so no tolerance was left. Each finishing operation on such a model was refused at the post.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins:\n- `crates/app/tests/model_fidelity_wide.rs`:\n  - `a_model_just_under_the_limit_posts_an_exact_finish_with_a_header_note` (0.019 mm).\n  - `a_model_just_over_the_limit_is_refused_by_name` (0.021 mm).\n  - `a_real_gouge_deeper_than_the_verdict_tolerance_still_blocks_a_widened_model` (0.02 mm under the face).\n  - `the_edge_gap_step_file_opened_at_reduced_accuracy_posts_a_face_with_the_note` (the #2994 fixture `edge_gap_018_stated_010.step`).\n  - `a_full_fidelity_model_and_a_mild_one_say_nothing_new`.\n- `crates/sim/tests/model_excess.rs`: `past_dev_tol_up_to_the_limit_only_the_promised_chord_is_taken`, `a_cut_deeper_than_the_widened_tolerance_into_a_convex_wall_is_still_convicted`.\n- `crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs`: a rotary op on a 0.019 mm model is still refused by name.\n\nMutation checks (each restored after):\n1. `excess_floor` takes the whole excess again: 2 app pins and 2 sim pins go red.\n2. `band_growth` reads the widened tolerance: `past_dev_tol_...` and `full_fidelity_grows_nothing` go red.\n3. The engine writes no notes: the header pin goes red.\n4. Every kind widens: the rotary pin goes red.\n\nPins changed on purpose (the old formula for a chord past `DEV_TOL`): `model_fidelity` (TIGHT), `fidelity_copies`, `coarse_probe_plasma` (plasma kerf), `import_step_edge_gap` (note text), and the sim `model_excess`, `coarse_collision` and `boundary_arc_walls`. The `coarse_collision` loops now use an excess past the limit. An excess of 0.01 mm is now judged, and those cases convict.\n\nFull-fidelity pins: unchanged and green.\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the head before the main merge: 254 steps, 2 red. Both were pins of the old formula, fixed in 5eef00704.\n- On the final head, the gate ran steps 1-128 (post, kernel, sim, motion) green. At step 129 (app build), the gate's sccache wrapper hung on `ring`'s `curve25519.c` two times. I stopped it.\n- I then ran the same binaries with plain cargo (`env -u RUSTC_WRAPPER`): all 601 `camcraft-app` lib and test binaries, and the 6 ui binaries that the gate selects. All green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) did not run. The change reaches them. This PR is not ready until they run.\n- No UI run. The model page shows the new sentence through `model_fidelity::summary`.\n- The bundled posts write the header note in their own `onComment` form. Only the default mill post is pinned.\n- Turning, rotary and probe kinds on a widened model are still refused. To judge them needs a separate collision allowance in those laws.\n- `model_fidelity.rs` is now 433 lines (it was 414 on main).\n\n## Overlaps\n\nEach of these touches the same file, in a different function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3037: `post/engine.rs` and `post/js_host.rs` (output budget, next to `ProgramId`).\n- #2893: `post/engine.rs` (fine-bore cycle arm).\n- #2836, #2714: `operation/probe_op.rs` (`stylus_cutter`).\n\nChangelog: A model opened at reduced accuracy (a chord error up to 0.02 mm) is now judged at its own accuracy, not refused: a finishing operation posts, and the program header and the model page name the tolerance that the checks used. Collision checks still allow for the whole deviation.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation).\n\nFixes #2996\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
